  "description": "KAMNAQ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C96 H90 Er6 N8 O26. From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er1B (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er2B (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er3B (Er) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.433-3.807 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 86.00-119.06°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C96H90Er6N8O26. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
